{"title":"1978 AHSME Problems/Problem 28","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_28\">Problem 28</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 28\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c9678bb6d237fcdff3e36abf130f908c0ffd296.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100); import cse5; pathpen=black; pair A1=(0,0), A2=(1,0), A3=(0.5,sqrt(3)/2); D(MP(&quot;A_1&quot;,A1)--MP(&quot;A_2&quot;,A2)--MP(&quot;A_3&quot;,A3,N)--cycle); pair A4=(A1+A2)/2, A5 = (A3+A2)/2, A6 = (A4+A3)/2; D(MP(&quot;A_4&quot;,A4,S)--MP(&quot;A_6&quot;,A6,W)--A3); D(A6--MP(&quot;A_5&quot;,A5,NE)--A4); //Credit to chezbgone2 for the diagram [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"602\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/4/78417453577b4c21be90756836f28e6c110d3877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle A_1A_2A_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> is equilateral and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1b5e3ec2f479f362661bebd80d01e211195a74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n+3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> is the midpoint of line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04d71635082231ff344631358090f79b2331853.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_nA_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, \nthen the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/14021dbd62bad13e2e97d55c8c9df55455da054e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle A_{44}A_{45}A_{43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/e/e6e55a8198a36139b393e82c8b92e243207df226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }30^\\circ\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }45^\\circ\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }60^\\circ\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }90^\\circ\\qquad  \\textbf{(E) }120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"444\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28Repeating_Cycles.2C_Kinda_.F0.9F.A7.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(Repeating_Cycles,_Kinda_🧀)\">Solution (Repeating Cycles, Kinda 🧀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (Repeating Cycles, Kinda 🧀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Upon graphing more points according to the rule mentioned in the problem, you can visibly see the rule repeats every 8 points (i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/627b08d5e5f4231d4f2d3c97247eb7ae99a8b947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/850174d5d0aefdb53a934cfffc7bf1f4f6d1372c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"17\" /> is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, etc.). Through very simple calculations, this means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa9c1ccad77c899ceb219e9573a686b58b981225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"17\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6f936abe426272c6ed7300a218f88be89175a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/1/94112488f9f334477f7b8dbcdc6da8774484bee4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"17\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef7fe0cf0006427ad470b8c83d13ee22d29ec0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/9557b4c51e078ad330306884abff5cb2ea6928d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"17\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791fe65c9d1ed7d8ed33a5025f40c5c7f9e476af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, and you can clearly see on the diagram that this is a 120 degree angle, leading to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62effaf0d5dc9bfa1d137bed40c4baa73698962d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" /> as the final answer.\n</p><p><br />\n~jackhu42_\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172746\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.018 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 73/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3661/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21509:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172746 and revision id 290759. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}